                  "The execution states the entry date, court, judgment amount, the applicable interest rate (and, where the 2% consumer-debt rate applies, that rate and the date it applies from) and the amount due, the parties, and the tenant's last known address; it reaches only property of, and debts owed to, a named judgment debtor who is not deceased (a deceased debtor: NY:CPLR-1203-1015-5208-parties); it carries the notices that $2,500 of an account holding identifiable exempt deposits and the 5222(i) wage-based amount are exempt. A judgment of a court other than the Supreme or County Court states the date its transcript was filed with the county clerk. It may be issued at any time before the judgment is satisfied or vacated, by the clerk or the creditor's attorney as officer of the court. It is returned within 60 days unless served under CPLR 5231 or 5232(a), extendable in writing by the attorney for up to 60 days at a time.",
